{{also|heid}}
==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|dum|nl}} ''-heit'' < {{etyl|odt|nl}} ''-heit'', {{proto|Germanic|haidus|lang=nl}}. Cognate with German {{term|-heit|lang=de}}, English {{term|-hood|lang=en}}.<ref>J. de Vries & F. de Tollenaere, "Etymologisch Woordenboek", Uitgeverij Het Spectrum, Utrecht, 1986 (14de druk)</ref>

===Suffix===
'''-heid''' {{f}} (''plural:'' '''[[-heden]]''')

# Converts an [[adjective]] into a [[noun]] and usually denotes an [[abstract]] [[quality]] of the adjectival [[root]]. It is often equivalent to the English suffix [[-ity]] or [[-ness]] but is cognate with the English suffix [[-hood]].

